    "result_text": "The full test suite passes. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the city-capacity rule for owner creation: creating an owner is rejected with **409** when the target city already contains **50 or more** owners.\n\nFollowing the project's OfficeFloor function-injection pattern (mirroring the existing `CheckHouseholdUnique` step), I added:\n\n1. **`CheckCityCapacity`** (`function/owner/`) \u2014 counts existing owners whose city matches the request's city (case-insensitive, trimmed) via `ownerRepository.findAll()`; throws a checked `CityAtCapacityException` when the count reaches 50.\n2. **`CityAtCapacityException`** (`escalation/`) \u2014 the checked exception carrying the city and count.\n3. **`CityAtCapacityExceptionHandler`** (`escalation/`) \u2014 responds `409 CONFLICT` with `{\"errors\":[\"city\"]}`, matching the shape used by `DuplicateHouseholdExceptionHandler`.\n4. **Escalation YAML** \u2014 `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.CityAtCapacityException.yml` wiring the exception to the handler.\n5. **Wired the step** into `owners.POST.yml` as `checkCityCapacity`, running under the transaction between `checkHousehold` and `build`.\n\n`AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity` (fills a fresh city to exactly 50, then expects the 51st to 409) passes, along with the rest of the suite (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
